[h1]Languages[/h1][url=https://lyuwenhan.github.io/extensions/minecraft-java/data/assets/auto-greeting/README/README.html]EN/English[/url] | [url=https://lyuwenhan.github.io/extensions/minecraft-java/data/assets/auto-greeting/README/README_ZH-CN.html]ZH-CN/简体中文[/url]
[h1]Auto Greeting[/h1]A Fabric mod that automatically sends preset greeting messages when [b]you[/b] or [b]other players[/b] join a server.
[h2]Features[/h2][list]
[*]Supports multiple messages[/*]
[*]Supports plain chat messages as well as commands[/*]
[*]Supports blacklist / whitelist rules for player names[/*]
[*]Supports placeholders[/*]
[*]Automatically sends preset messages after [b]you[/b] join a server[/*]
[*]Automatically sends preset messages when [b]other players[/b] join a server[/*]
[/list][h2]Command Overview[/h2][list]
[*][b]/autogreet self ...[/b][/*]
[*][b]/autogreet other ...[/b][/*]
[/list]Notes:
[list]
[*][b][a|b][/b] means [b]a[/b] or [b]b[/b][/*]
[/list]For example:
[code]/autogreet [other|self] status[/code]
means either:
[code]/autogreet other status[/code]
or
[code]/autogreet self status[/code]
[h2]Commands[/h2][h3]Status[/h3]Controls whether auto greeting is [b]enabled[/b] or [b]disabled[/b].
[code]/autogreet [self|other] status
/autogreet [self|other] status enable
/autogreet [self|other] status disable
/autogreet [self|other] status toggle[/code]
[h3]Message[/h3]Controls the messages sent by the mod.
Placeholders are supported.
[code]/autogreet [self|other] message add <message>
/autogreet [self|other] message add <message> <index>
/autogreet [self|other] message remove
/autogreet [self|other] message remove <index>
/autogreet [self|other] message remove all
/autogreet [self|other] message list[/code]
[h4]Placeholders for [b]self[/b][/h4][table]
[tbody]
[tr]
[th]Placeholder[/th]
[th]Description[/th]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td][b]@player[/b][/td]
[td]Player name[/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td][b]@UUID[/b][/td]
[td]UUID[/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td][b]@X[/b][/td]
[td]X coordinate (up to 3 decimals)[/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td][b]@Y[/b][/td]
[td]Y coordinate (up to 3 decimals)[/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td][b]@Z[/b][/td]
[td]Z coordinate (up to 3 decimals)[/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td][b]@health[/b][/td]
[td]Current health[/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td][b]@level[/b][/td]
[td]Current experience level[/td]
[/tr]
[/tbody]
[/table]
[h4]Placeholders for [b]other[/b][/h4][table]
[tbody]
[tr]
[th]Placeholder[/th]
[th]Description[/th]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td][b]@player[/b][/td]
[td]Player name[/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td][b]@UUID[/b][/td]
[td]Player UUID[/td]
[/tr]
[/tbody]
[/table]
[h3]Blacklist / Whitelist[/h3][code]/autogreet other [whitelist|blacklist] list
/autogreet other [whitelist|blacklist] clear confirm

/autogreet other [whitelist|blacklist] [match|except] list

/autogreet other [whitelist|blacklist] [match|except] [equal|contain|startWith|endWith] add <pattern>
/autogreet other [whitelist|blacklist] [match|except] [equal|contain|startWith|endWith] remove
/autogreet other [whitelist|blacklist] [match|except] [equal|contain|startWith|endWith] remove <index>
/autogreet other [whitelist|blacklist] [match|except] [equal|contain|startWith|endWith] remove all
/autogreet other [whitelist|blacklist] [match|except] [equal|contain|startWith|endWith] list[/code]
[h2]Examples[/h2][code]/autogreet self message add Hello, I'm @player at (@X, @Y, @Z)
/autogreet self message add HP: @health | Level: @level

/autogreet other message add Welcome @player!
/autogreet other message add Hello @player (@UUID)[/code]
[h2]Message Behavior[/h2]If a message starts with [b]/[/b], it is executed as a command.
If a message does not start with [b]/[/b], it is sent as a normal chat message.
[h2]Filtering[/h2][b]other[/b] greetings support:
[list]
[*]blacklist[/*]
[*]whitelist[/*]
[*][b]match[/b] rules[/*]
[*][b]except[/b] rules[/*]
[*][b]equal[/b][/*]
[*][b]contain[/b][/*]
[*][b]startWith[/b][/*]
[*][b]endWith[/b][/*]
[/list]These rules determine whether the name of a joining player should trigger greeting logic.
[h3]Filtering behavior[/h3][list]
[*]If a player matches the [b]blacklist[/b], they are ignored[/*]
[*]If a player matches the blacklist but also matches [b]blacklist except[/b], they are allowed again[/*]
[*]If the [b]whitelist[/b] is not empty, only players matching the whitelist are allowed[/*]
[*]If a player matches the whitelist but also matches [b]whitelist except[/b], they are ignored[/*]
[/list][h2]Notes[/h2][list]
[*][b]index[/b] is optional and 1-based[/*]
[*][b]add <message> <index>[/b] inserts before the existing item at that position[/*]
[*]If [b]index[/b] is omitted or outside the valid range, the message is appended[/*]
[*][b]remove <index>[/b] removes the specified item[/*]
[*][b]remove[/b] without an index removes the last item[/*]
[*][b]remove all[/b] clears the message list[/*]
[*][b]clear confirm[/b] clears the entire blacklist or whitelist rule set[/*]
[*]Numeric values are formatted with up to 3 decimal places, and trailing zeros are removed[/*]
[/list][h2]Supported Versions[/h2][list]
[*]Minecraft 26.1.2[/*]
[*]Fabric Loader 0.19.2+[/*]
[*]Fabric API 0.150.0+[/*]
[*]Java 25[/*]
[*]Cloth config (Optional)[/*]
[*]Modmenu (Optional)[/*]
[/list][h2]License[/h2]MIT
